efault to `True` in 3.0.\r\n\r\nSo now it defaults to `True`. Every `@asgi` handler (mounted or nt mounted) will gets a copy of the scope, so top-level keys it adds or replaces no longer leak into the outer scope. The copy is shallow, so nested values like `scope[\"state\"]` are still shared.\r\n\r\nRemoved both deprecation warnings, one at registration and one at request time.\r\n\r\nIf a mounted app is *meant* to talk to the outer app through the scope, pass `copy_scope=False`. That behaviour is unchanged.\r\n\r\nBreaking for anyone relying on the old pass-through default without having set `copy_scope=False` explicitly, and it now fails silently, since the warning that used to flag it is gone.\r\n\r\n<!-- docs-preview -->\n\n<hr>\n📚 Documentation preview 📚: <a href=\"https://litestar-org.github.io/litestar-docs-preview/5164\">https://litestar-org.github.io/litestar-docs-preview/5164</a> \n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:43Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T12:46:58Z","closed_at":"2026-10-30T12:46:57Z","merged_at":"2026-10-30T12:46:57Z","merge_commit_sha":"716f8b023b1c13e6f1e8ab08dfa1938f7923312d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"litestar-org:v3/copy-scope-default-true","ref":"v3/copy-scope-default-true","repo":{"id":435625572,"node_id":"R_kgDOGfceZA","name":"litestar","full_name":"litestar-org/litestar","owner":{"login":"litestar-org","id":97250344,"node_id":"O_kgDOBcvsKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97250344?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org","html_url":"https://github.com/litestar-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/litestar-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subs